prompt.text:
Repair the CommonJS module below and return one corrected complete source file. It must export exactly `{ drawRoute }`.

`drawRoute(width, height, points)` returns an array of `height` strings, each exactly `width` characters. Empty cells are `.`, and each listed point is drawn as `#`. `width` and `height` must be integers from 1 through 1000. `points` must be an array of plain objects with integer `x` and `y` coordinates, where `0 <= x < width` and `0 <= y < height`. Duplicate points are valid and have no additional effect. An empty points array returns a blank grid. Throw `TypeError` for malformed dimensions, containers, points, or coordinates. Validate all points before constructing the output. Do not mutate `points` or its objects.

Known-bad source:
```javascript
function drawRoute(width, height, points) {
  if (!Number.isInteger(width) || width < 1 || width > 1000 ||
      !Number.isInteger(height) || height < 1 || height > 1000 ||
      !Array.isArray(points)) {
    throw new TypeError('invalid arguments');
  }
  for (const point of points) {
    if (point === null || typeof point !== 'object' || Array.isArray(point) ||
        !Number.isInteger(point.x) || !Number.isInteger(point.y) ||
        point.x < 0 || point.x >= height || point.y < 0 || point.y >= height) {
      throw new TypeError('invalid point');
    }
  }

  const grid = Array.from({ length: height }, () => Array(width).fill('.'));
  for (const point of points) grid[point.y][point.x] = '#';
  return grid.map((row) => row.join(''));
}

module.exports = { drawRoute };
```

